{
    "chapter_num": 4,
    "verses_count": 17,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Friendship with the World"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "What causes wars, and what causes fightings among you? Is it not your passions that are at war in your members? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "You desire and do not have; so you kill. And you covet"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or you kill and you covet"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and cannot obtain; so you fight and wage war. You do not have, because you do not ask. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "You ask and do not receive, because you ask wrongly, to spend it on your passions. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Unfaithful creatures! Do you not know that friendship with the world is enmity with God? Therefore whoever wishes to be a friend of the world makes himself an enemy of God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Or do you suppose it is in vain that the scripture says, “He yearns jealously over the spirit which he has made to dwell in us”? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But he gives more grace; therefore it says, “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil and he will flee from you. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Draw near to God and he will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you men of double mind. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Be wretched and mourn and weep. Let your laughter be turned to mourning and your joy to dejection. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Humble yourselves before the Lord and he will exalt you."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Warning against Judging Another"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Do not speak evil against one another, brethren. He that speaks evil against a brother or judges his brother, speaks evil against the law and judges the law. But if you judge the law, you are not a doer of the law but a judge. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "There is one lawgiver and judge, he who is able to save and to destroy. But who are you that you judge your neighbor?"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Boasting about Tomorrow"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go into such and such a town and spend a year there and trade and get gain”; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "whereas you do not know about tomorrow. What is your life? For you are a mist that appears for a little time and then vanishes. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Instead you ought to say, “If the Lord wills, we shall live and we shall do this or that.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "As it is, you boast in your arrogance. All such boasting is evil. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Whoever knows what is right to do and fails to do it, for him it is sin."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}